# .codespell-ignore — words codespell flags but we use intentionally.
#
# One word per line. Codespell matches these against its misspelling
# dictionary, so each entry suppresses the suggested "correction".
#
# File-type extensions that collide with English words:
als
caf
edn
sav
# Package-lock JSON noise:
Nd
# Rust keyword (codespell thinks it's "create"):
crate
# Valid English variant; we use "unparseable" (cannot be parsed) over
# codespell's preferred "unparsable":
unparseable
